{"nodes": [{"id": "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_sketch_tradeoff", "label": "Sketches Store a Function of the Data, Not the Data", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/probabilistic-data-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Mental Model", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Give up exactness and space collapses from proportional-to-the-data to proportional-to-the-accuracy-you-asked-for. Three checks in order: which direction does the error go, is it mergeable, does the bound hold in practice."}, {"id": "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_bloom_filter", "label": "Bloom Filter", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/probabilistic-data-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Bloom filter \u2014 sizing is the whole design", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One-sided error: all k bits set means maybe present, any bit clear means definitely absent \u2014 because insertion only ever sets bits, which is also why you cannot delete. Measured FP matched theory to within 0.01 percentage points; ~4.8 bits/item divides the FP rate by 10. Space is independent of item size but NOT of n, so it saturates silently on an unbounded stream."}, {"id": "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_double_hashing", "label": "Double Hashing (Kirsch-Mitzenmacher)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/probabilistic-data-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Bloom filter mechanics", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "h1 + i*h2 gives k independent-enough hashes from two; computing k real hashes is wasted work and the asymptotic FP rate is unaffected."}, {"id": "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_hyperloglog", "label": "HyperLogLog", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/probabilistic-data-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "HyperLogLog", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each register stores a MAXIMUM number of leading zeros, so it is idempotent \u2014 which is exactly what makes it count distinct items and what makes it merge by element-wise max. Measured: 16 KB (p=14) counted 10,000,000 distinct to 0.41%, and the memory is identical for 1,000 or 10 billion."}, {"id": "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_count_min_sketch", "label": "Count-Min Sketch", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/probabilistic-data-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "The Invariant", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "d rows of w counters; the estimate min_i sketch[i][h_i(x)] only ever over-estimates because collisions only add. Safe for heavy hitters ('definitely at least this frequent'), unsafe for 'is this rare'."}, {"id": "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_cuckoo_filter", "label": "Cuckoo Filter", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/probabilistic-data-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "The family", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stores fingerprints in a cuckoo hash table: supports deletion natively and is often smaller than a Bloom below ~1% FP. The modern default when deletion is needed, at the cost of an insertion failure mode near full and a weaker merge story."}, {"id": "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_mergeability", "label": "Mergeability (Merge Sketches, Then Query)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/probabilistic-data-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Pitfalls in Depth", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Distinct-count and quantiles are not linear functionals, so estimates cannot be summed or averaged. Merging must happen on the sketch representation where the mathematics is defined: HLL by element-wise max (exact), Bloom by OR, Count-Min by add. Ship the sketch, not the estimate \u2014 and all hosts must agree on parameters, which becomes a versioning problem."}, {"id": "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_t_digest", "label": "t-digest / DDSketch (Mergeable Quantiles)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/probabilistic-data-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "The family / Use Cases", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bounded relative error in Theta(1/eps) space, accurate at the tails, and mergeable \u2014 the only correct way to get a global p99 from per-host data."}], "edges": [{"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_bloom_filter", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_sketch_tradeoff", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/probabilistic-data-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Mental Model", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_hyperloglog", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_sketch_tradeoff", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/probabilistic-data-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Mental Model", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_count_min_sketch", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_sketch_tradeoff", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/probabilistic-data-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "The Invariant", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_bloom_filter", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_double_hashing", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/probabilistic-data-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Bloom filter mechanics", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_cuckoo_filter", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_bloom_filter", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/probabilistic-data-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Pitfall: Deleting from a standard Bloom filter", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_mergeability", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_hyperloglog", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/probabilistic-data-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Pitfalls in Depth", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_mergeability", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_t_digest", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/probabilistic-data-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Pitfalls in Depth", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_mergeability", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_selection_and_order_statistics_learning_never_average_percentiles", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/probabilistic-data-structures/learning.md", "source_location": "Pitfall: Averaging or naively combining sketches \u2014 links ../selection-and-order-statistics/learning.md", "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": [{"id": "one_sided_error_and_mergeability_govern_sketch_use", "label": "Error Direction + Mergeability Govern Every Sketch's Safe Use", "nodes": ["data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_bloom_filter", "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_hyperloglog", "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_count_min_sketch", "data_structures_and_algorithms_probabilistic_data_structures_learning_mergeability", "data_structures_and_algorithms_selection_and_order_statistics_learning_never_average_percentiles"], "relation": "participate_in", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/probabilistic-data-structures/learning.md"}]}